# 14. Explain Atomicity, Consistency, Isolation, and Durability.

### Atomicity

```text
All succeed
OR
All fail
```

### Consistency

Database rules and constraints remain satisfied.

### Isolation

Concurrent transactions are controlled so intermediate or conflicting states aren't improperly exposed.

### Durability

After a successful commit, changes are designed to survive system failures.

### 🎤 Strong interview answer

> Atomicity ensures a transaction is treated as one unit. Consistency ensures database rules remain satisfied. Isolation controls the interaction between concurrent transactions. Durability ensures committed changes persist despite failures.

